---
// Starlight's two-column layout (content plus a right-hand table of contents) without its
// column arithmetic. Below 100rem the content is one column beside the left sidebar and the
// table of contents is the dropdown at the top of it; from 100rem the table of contents is the
// fixed column of PageSidebar.astro, and styles/layout.css keeps its width free at the right of
// every documentation page, whether the page has a list or not, so the text does not move
// between pages. The content column itself is left to ContentPanel (centred in the space
// that is left).
// Copied from @astrojs/starlight 0.42.10, dist/components/TwoColumnContent.astro; on an update,
// diff it against the new original (PageSidebar.astro is the other file). It relies on the
// `right-sidebar` slot that Starlight's Page.astro fills. The CSS that relies on Starlight's
// internals is listed at the top of styles/layout.css.
// Upgrade note: the default component also positions the right column and narrows the main
// pane for it, with its own breakpoint (72rem); none of that applies here.
---

<div class="ritueel-main">
  {Astro.locals.starlightRoute.toc && <slot name="right-sidebar" />}
  <div class="main-pane"><slot /></div>
</div>

<style>
  @layer starlight.core {
    .main-pane {
      isolation: isolate;
      width: 100%;
      /* The content column is left to ContentPanel: a column of --sl-content-width
         centred in the space beside the sidebar. */
      min-width: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
